# Complete Library Workflow Example
# This demonstrates a full library use case from start to finish

### 1. Login as librarian
# The first librarian is created on startup from LIBRARY_ADMIN_* in .env
POST http://localhost:8080/admin/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username = admin &
password = change-me

###

### 2. Create another librarian
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/librarians
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "librarian1",
  "password": "secret123"
}

###

### 3. Create a book
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "1984",
  "publicationYear": 1984,
  "isbn": "9789876543210",
  "authorNames": [
    "George Orwell"
  ]
}

###

### 4. Create copies of the book
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookIsbn": "9789876543210",
  "quantity": 3
}

###

### 5. Create a customer at the desk (no account yet)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Joe",
  "lastName": "Mama",
  "email": "joe.mama@example.com"
}

> {% client.global.set("customerId", response.body.id); %}

###

### 6. Generate an activation code and hand it to the customer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/customers/{{customerId}}/activation-code

> {% client.global.set("activationCode", response.body.activationCode); %}

###

### 7. Customer registers online with the code
POST http://localhost:8080/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "activationCode": "{{activationCode}}",
  "username": "customer1",
  "password": "customer123"
}

###

### 8. Login as customer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username = customer1 &
password = customer123

###

### 9. Customer browses books (public endpoint)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/search?q=1984

###

### 10. Customer checks book details (including available copies)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/9789876543210

###

### 11. Customer reserves a copy
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookIsbn": "9789876543210"
}

###

### 12. Customer checks their reservations
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/mine

###

### 13. Login back as librarian for checkout
POST http://localhost:8080/admin/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username = librarian1 &
password = secret123

###

### 14. Librarian checks out the reserved copy
POST http://localhost:8080/api/desk/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "copyId": 1,
  "customerId": {{customerId}}
}

###

### 15. Librarian processes return
POST http://localhost:8080/api/desk/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "copyId": 1,
  "customerId": {{customerId}}
}

###

### 16. Check book details to see available copies are 3 again
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/9789876543210